if i think big  i'm gonna have to spend more  that's a common  thought that a lot of entrepreneurs have  and one that came in to me from one of  my youtube viewers rosie  roses open up a shop in north london two  months away and  wants to grow this thing wants to have a  lot of success with her business and is  wondering should i start small or should  i think big  but thinking big is going to cost me a  lot more money  here's the thing this is this is so  important to understand  you want to think big  but you need to act small  you think big because that's what  keeps you going that's what keeps it  going through all the crap when things  get really hard with your business you  have a big vision of of what you want  the world to look like and how you want  people to use your products and services  and the impact and the money you're  gonna have  that's that's what drives you but you  start small  here's why it's so important okay if you  think big and you act big from the start  and you go out and you take out  a loan  right and you really use this money to  buy a huge store not just this little  store but you get a bigger store or  multiple stores and then you need to  market it and you take out  advertisements on the radio and tv and  and leafleting and everything you do to  create this business and you hire staff  you take out this huge loan to make this  happen the chances  of you making it are tiny  it's possible  but it's tiny  the reason is when you first start a  business you're gonna make a ton  of incorrect assumptions okay you're  going to write in your business plan  that you think you know you're going to  do this and then this is going to happen  it almost never works out that way if  you look at most successful companies  the idea that they started with at the  very beginning of what they thought the  company would look like is never how it  actually turns out  so the danger in going big too quickly  is that you spend all this money and  time  going in a direction  that is going to fail  because you're not only making one  mistake at a time you're making hundreds  of mistakes at a time and so the chances  of that working out is minuscule  where it's better  to start on a small scale  start making your mistakes one at a time  start by testing your different  marketing levers and seeing what works  and when you figured out something that  is working for you if it's radio ads if  it's leafleting if it's partnerships  whatever it is that is starting to drive  sales for you then you invest into  making that bigger and then bigger and  bigger and bigger  i encourage entrepreneurs to think big  because a lot of us have a limited  belief that we're only so good we can  only have so much of an impact we don't  see ourselves as being great  and i see a lot of greatness within a  ton of entrepreneurs and it frustrates  me that they don't see it within  themselves they don't have the  confidence to really build up  their business is something that can  really help a lot of people  so when i say think big  that's what i'm talking about it  frustrates me to always work with  entrepreneurs who don't believe in  themselves  but when it comes to actually executing  your plan  you start small you have you're thinking  big but you're starting small step by  step  testing your assumptions making your  mistakes with this  little negative outcome that can come  from it  you prove to yourself that this can work  and then expand from there and the sky  literally is the limit and if you do it  that way  you think big but you start small  your chances of success go up  dramatically and that's what i want for  you because i don't want to see you take  on a huge loan because evan said think  big and end up failing and have this  crushing debt over you for the rest of  your life and be afraid to get back in  the business because your first one  didn't work out and was so painful  it's possible it's possible to have a  huge  massively successful company  and it starts with combining thinking  big  with starting small  belief  if you like this video please give it a  thumbs up below and i want to hear you  have to think leave a comment underneath  let me know what's on your mind let me  know what questions you have for your  company i'll make a video response thank  you so much and i'll see you soon

